ist Shot Wide Left","type":{"id":"507","text":"Missed","abbreviation":"shot-missed"},"clock":{"displayValue":"0:47"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"17"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5349","displayName":"Nazem Kadri","shortName":"N. Kadri"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"5571","displayName":"Sergei Bobrovsky","shortName":"S. Bobrovsky"}}]},{"id":"401892683000000080","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Goalie Stopped","type":{"id":"516","text":"Stoppage","abbreviation":"stoppage"},"clock":{"displayValue":"0:50"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}},{"id":"401892683000000660","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"John Tavares faceoff won against Nazem Kadri","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"0:50"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"21"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5160","displayName":"John Tavares","shortName":"J. Tavares"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"5349","displayName":"Nazem Kadri","shortName":"N. Kadri"}}]},{"id":"401892683000000740","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Gabriel Landeskog hit Chris Tanev","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:05"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"17"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"2562609","displayName":"Gabriel Landeskog","shortName":"G. Landeskog"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"5592","displayName":"Chris Tanev","shortName":"C. Tanev"},"type":"hitted"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1838","fullName":"Scotiabank Arena","address":{"city":"Toronto","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1838.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18853,"officials":[{"fullName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","displayName":"Frederick L'Ecuyer","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Matt MacPherson","displayName":"Matt MacPherson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Tyson Baker","displayName":"Tyson Baker","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Michael Markovic","displayName":"Michael Markovic","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Landeskog scores twice and the Avalanche hand the Maple Leafs their 4th straight loss, 6-3","description":"— Gabriel Landeskog scored his second goal of the game early in the third period to put the Colorado Avalanche ahead for good in a 6-3 win over the Toronto Maple Leafs on Tuesday night.","story":"TORONTO -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562609/gabriel-landeskog\">Gabriel Landeskog</a> scored his second goal of the game early in the third period to put the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/col/colorado-avalanche\">Colorado Avalanche</a> ahead for good in a 6-3 win over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tor/toronto-maple-leafs\">Toronto Maple Leafs</a> on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3096249/devon-toews\">Devon Toews</a>, with a goal and an assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5798/brock-nelson\">Brock Nelson</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042050/artturi-lehkonen\">Artturi Lehkonen</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233586/martin-necas\">Martin Necas</a> in an empty net also scored for Colorado. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233563/cale-makar\">Cale Makar</a> added two assists and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904177/mackenzie-blackwood\">Mackenzie Blackwood</a> made 28 saves. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3149843/darren-raddysh\">Darren Raddysh</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149211/easton-cowan\">Easton Cowan</a>, with a goal and an assist each, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3904098/jack-roslovic\">Jack Roslovic</a> scored for Toronto, which has lost four games in a row and dropped six of its last seven.\n\n\r\n              Sergei Bobrovksy finished with 22 stops.\n\n\r\n              The 38-year-old goaltender — a two-time Stanley Cup champion and two-time Vezina Trophy winner as the NHL’s top netminder — has allowed three goals or more in 12 of his 13 starts since signing in free agency July 1.\n\n\r\n              Landeskog scored the go-ahead goal at 5:02 of the third, just 51 seconds after Roslovic tied the score 3-3.\n\n\r\n              Raddysh’s blast that gave Toronto a 1-0 lead was clocked at 92.89 miles per hour — the fourth fastest shot to result in a goal across the league this season, according to the NHL.\n\n\r\n              Roslovic (lower-body injury) and shutdown defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5592/chris-tanev\">Chris Tanev</a> (load management) returned to the Toronto lineup after sitting out Sunday’s 4-0 loss to the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976833/morgan-rielly\">Morgan Rielly</a> (lower-body injury) joined a long list of players receiving treatment in the trainer’s room. The veteran blueliner is listed as day-to-day, while center <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2993474/colton-sissons\">Colton Sissons</a> (lower-body injury) is week-to-week. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587996/kirill-marchenko\">Kirill Marchenko</a> (lower body) along with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4419778/marshall-rifai\">Marshall Rifai</a> (lower body) and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4781550/nick-blankenburg\">Nick Blankenburg</a> (upper body) also remain sidelined and week-to-week.\n\n\r\n              Makar left Sunday’s practice in Denver with an unspecified injury, but took part in Colorado’s morning skate and declared himself ready for Tuesday.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Avalanche: At the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ott/ottawa-senators\">Ottawa Senators</a> on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Maple Leafs: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/min/minnesota-wild\">Minnesota Wild</a> on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-11T02:59:34Z"}}